#254 (F212) round 2 of 2 (C34): the reviewer BLOCKed head 92ce117 with R254-001..005 (verdict: pij-governance/.harness/government/community/roles/reviewer/outputs/2026-11/19-verdict-pr-254-92ce117.dd.json). Worktree ~/pi-hacking/fleet-f212, branch fix/f212-copilot-auth-restart. All five fixes go out in ONE push, then pr-freeze, then FINAL to pij-steady-otter with the new head and the regression test names.

DONE (uncommitted, not built):
- auth_recovery.rs rewritten:
  - Ledger in Services (`pub(crate) auth_recovery: Arc<auth_recovery::Ledger>`, built in lib.rs) holds a per-seat tokio Mutex<Option<Entry>> (R254-003).
  - The window is an Instant RECOVERY_WINDOW of 30 min (R254-002). After a daemon restart, remembered() rebuilds the entry from the latest seat.auth_recovery spine event; its wall-clock age is used only to spare.
  - New Action::NotRestarted: the restart control is no longer live (queue.live_payloads of delivery-control:<seat> has no row with its msg_id) and the same incarnation reports again, so tell parent+primes it didn't take (/exit then `pij revive`) (R254-001). A Refused receipt from accept_control becomes Notify.
  - decide(last, now: Instant, reporter: Incarnation, settled, free).
  - recipients = live parent + designated prime of each project from try_holdings_of → watchdogs().project(p).prime_id, deduped, never the seat; machine singleton prime removed (R254-005).
- http/auth_error.rs: the request now requires pid + proc_start; it must equal seat.proc, else 409 E-RS-AUTH-STALE (R254-004).
- store.mjs sends {...this.tuple(), kind}; the store.test.mjs expectation is updated (F212 extension tests pass).

TODO:
1. Rewrite crates/daemon/src/auth_recovery_tests.rs for the new API, handle(services, seat, reporter: Incarnation{pid:4100, proc_start:7}, kind, now_ms). Tests:
   - idle restart; busy notify; draft notify;
   - same incarnation while the control is live → Pending;
   - after claiming and acking the control job (queue.claim + ack Outcome::Done/Failed) → NotRestarted with a notice;
   - new incarnation → Relogin, then Told;
   - concurrent tokio::join! of two reports → exactly one Restart and one Pending, one control queued;
   - a wall-clock jump (+2h now_ms) still Pending (monotonic);
   - project prime told (insert projects row via services.store_pools[0] like idle_nudge_tests::the_projects_designated_prime_gets_the_fyi, plus a holding via watchdogs().record_assignment_committed), deduped against the parent;
   - fresh Ledger (simulated daemon restart) + spine record → not a second Restart;
   - update the decide() unit test to the Instant API.
2. tests/copilot_compact.rs: report_lost_login must send pid 920_002, proc_start 9 (the copilot() fixture's proc). Add a stale-pid test (409, no control).
3. Docs: pij-rs-api.md F212 section (request now has pid, proc_start; actions add not-restarted; window monotonic; recipients = parent + project primes); copilot-native-extension.md wording; D-F212-1 if needed.
4. Build ONCE: `PIJ_SHARED_TARGET=<abs>/fleet-f212/target just shared-build -- fmt ... --then test -p pij-daemon --lib auth_recovery --then test -p pij-daemon --test copilot_compact`. fleet-f210/target was deleted at the PM's request, so it's a fresh build. Disk sits near the 25 GiB floor: check df first, never override, leave the rest to CI.
5. biome format the .mjs files; just lint, just typecheck; `env -u NO_COLOR -u FORCE_COLOR harness checks --quick`; commit (Delivers: none / Fixes: F212); push; edit the PR body (round 2 section listing the R254 fixes and regression names); just pr-freeze 254; FINAL to pij-steady-otter.
